coder › Done on branch `work/env-config` (3 commits).

What changed:
- `src/env.ts` (new): `fromEnv(env, prefix='APP_'): Partial<Config>` reads `APP_PORT/APP_HOST/APP_DEBUG/APP_NAME`. Absent (`undefined`) or empty (`''`) left out; port via `Number()` (`NaN` → `TypeError("<KEY> must be a number")`); debug case-insensitive `true/1/yes` → true, `false/0/no` → false, else `TypeError("<KEY> must be a boolean")`; host/name as strings. Key names include the prefix, so a custom prefix is named too.
- `src/config.ts`: added `validate(config): Config` returning the same object, else `TypeError` naming the field: port not an integer 1–65535, host empty, name empty.
- `src/index.ts`: `resolveConfig(file = {}, env = process.env)` = `validate(merge(merge(DEFAULTS, file), fromEnv(env)))`, so file over defaults, env over both.
- Tests: `src/env.test.ts` (read all four, absent/empty omitted, debug variants, custom prefix, both TypeErrors), `src/config.test.ts` (valid returns same ref, bad ports 0/-1/65536/1.5/NaN, empty host/name), extended `src/index.test.ts` (env beats file/defaults, invalid file or env throws).

Decisions not in the plan: `fromEnv` accepts any numeric port (e.g. `1.5`) and leaves integer/range to `validate`; error messages are `"<VAR> must be a number/boolean"` and `"port must be an integer between 1 and 65535"`, `"host/name must not be empty"`; only exact `''` counts as empty (whitespace goes through normal parsing/validation).

